  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (3000€) and then comparing the probabilities of exceeding this level. Lottery B has a 45% chance of exceeding it (6000 > 3000), while Lottery A has 0%. The reason would thus prefer Lottery B. However, the individual chooses Lottery A and justifies this based on risk aversion and the high probability of winning a 'decent' amount. The individual considers the outcomes and probabilities but does not reference any aggregation of outcomes across lotteries to form a reference point, nor do they evaluate which lottery exceeds a shared benchmark more frequently. There is no evidence of computing or reasoning about differences from an aspiration level of 3000€. Instead, the justification is based on maximizing the chance of winning, not on aspiration-based differences. Therefore, the cognitive mechanism described in the decision reason is not reflected in the verbal report.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
